      'An implicit wait is a session setting: every find element keeps looking for up to that time. An explicit wait, such as WebDriverWait, checks a condition you choose, every 500 ms by default in Java and Python, until it holds or the timeout passes. Mixing them makes each check of the explicit wait block for the implicit time, so waits become unpredictable. The documentation says not to mix them.',
      '<p>With an implicit wait of 10 s and an explicit wait of 15 s for an element that never comes, the wait gives up after about 20.5 s, not 15.</p>',
